I am having an issue using the qca988x firmware on Linux with kernel
4.2. We are using this firmware on a Compex WLE900VX wifi card to
create a wireless access point. After about a day of uptime, the
wireless device goes down and prints to dmesg (see attatched).  I am
fairly certain the issue is occurring is the firmware, since the wifi
card cannot be brought back up, even after reloading the driver
entirely. Does anyone have any idea what the issue may be or how to
fix it?

Thanks for any help and I can provide more information as needed,
Tom Caputi

